From the k306 design pass (choices worker, 2026-10-31; $S/w-choices306/design.md, findings F3 and F4).

F4: the network, registry, cilium and ssl accessors in OCP::Config return the raw spec value. `network: foo` (a string where a mapping belongs) crashes inside Perl in ocp node add, ocp deploy-robocop and ocp update, which read it without validate().

F3: the accessors that already refuse a bad shape in validate()s words (kubernetes, gpu_config, ssh_config, system_config, the switches, and _first_cp_string) use croak. A croak carries " at FILE line N.", so where no validate() runs first, OCP.pm labels the line "This is an internal error. Run again with --verbose". Example: ocp update with gpu: false. Same family as k375 (wrong PIN1).

Done =
- the four sections refuse a wrong shape in validate()s words, as gpu_config does;
- every refusing accessor dies with "line\n" (no location, no internal-error label) instead of croak;
- validate() keeps each line exactly once (shared producers, as k306 step 1 sets up);
- tests: one malformed shape per section through a command that reads it without validate(), and the output must not match / at \S+ line \d+|internal error|HASH\(0x|ARRAY\(0x/. Red first, then a mutation check.

Lane: ocp-choices-worker, after k306 step 1 (spec_errors and its producers) has landed. Coordinate with k306 step 3a, which converts name/control_planes/workers the same way.

